  user_input {
    user_response: "did you already created the app? these are supporting details --- please generate a professional prompt for google ai studio to create an android app named MedsAlarm it\'s a one pager app but with splash screen containing the app logo and the app title which is MedsAlarm and a subtitle \"Medication Reminders Made Simple\" that will show in 3 seconds before the main home screen. the app should not be a web app but a native kotlin java that utilizes the phone notification on the status bar even if the app is closed it will notify the user thru alarm, also utilize the sound alarm and the vibrate alarm on the phone native so that even if the app is closed it will fire once the set time is met. the main page should have a top navigation bar that contains the app icon, the app title, the app subtitle \"Medication Reminders Made Simple\" with a \"Today is <day of the week>, mmmm, dd, yyyy | hh:mm:ss AM/PM\" compressed in one line. use the mv3 colors of the screen. it should contain a big \"+\" icon on the bottom right of the screen. there is no bottom navigation bar. below the top navigation bar, contains a list of alarms set that user can scroll. scrolling does not move the top navigation bar and the big \"+\" icon on the bottom right of the screen. compress the list so that many list can be seen at once. do not duplicate lists (example, 3 lists) for a med that is 3x a day. on the list it should show the Medicine Name then below it a smaller text to display frequency (e.g. 1 Tab 3X a Day) and below another text that says the status (e.g. 2 Done, 1 Pending) and on the right of the list shows a button to take the med. so once the 3x completed within the current day, the background color of the list will be light green and the button disappers in the list with dark green text saying \"Done\". take note the home screen lists will only show the list of meds for the current day, it will refresh again tomorrow (so the done yesterday will be undone the next day). on the \"+\" screen the user can set an alarm with textboxes Medicine Name, Dosage (with hints e.g. 3 mg), Instruction (optional), Medication Form with icon choices (tablet, capsule, injection), and then time spinner option with AM/PM (same with the phone UI when setting time alarms) and Repeat Days selection just S, M, T, W, T, F, S buttons) and Dose Time (e.g. 2x, 3x, 5x a day) it will automatically calculate and set the succeeding time based on the time set (e.g. 2x a day so a day is 24 hours the computation answer is it will get +12 hours for the next dose) and then a 3 checkboxes for notifications (Status Bar Notification, Sound Alarm, Vibrate Alarm) again it it will access the native phone feature so that even if the app is closed it will fire the alarm. then a set button. once clicked the set button it will show the list in the home screen. also every list should have a countdown timer HH:MM:SS for the next take of meds.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_START]\nInstructions: If you need more context from the user you must first ask the user some questions using the ask_question tool. If you ask questions, you must wait for the user\'s answers. After the questions you must present a plan.\n[AIS_METADATA_SECTION_END]"
